## 3.5 Change History

### Purpose

The Change History section records the chronological history of approved modifications made to a System Objective throughout its lifecycle.

Its purpose is to preserve engineering decisions, maintain historical accountability, and support traceability across all approved revisions.

---

### Standard Fields

Every System Objective shall include the following change history fields:

| Field | Description |
|--------|-------------|
| Change Identifier | Unique identifier for the approved change record. |
| Version Affected | Version introduced by the approved change. |
| Change Date | Date the change became effective. |
| Change Classification | Editorial, Minor Engineering, or Major Engineering. |
| Change Summary | Concise description of the approved change. |
| Engineering Justification | Reason for the approved change. |
| Approval Reference | Reference to the approval authorizing the change. |

---

### Change History Rules

Change history shall:

- Record only approved changes.
- Be maintained in chronological order.
- Preserve all historical records.
- Never remove or overwrite previous approved entries.
- Remain consistent with the Objective Governance framework.

---

### Engineering Note

The Change History section provides a permanent record of the evolution of a System Objective.

It supports engineering accountability by documenting what changed, why it changed, when it changed, and under whose authority.
